  },
  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you've put in the effort to paint your interior trim, only for it to start peeling shortly after! Often, this comes down to a few common culprits. One big one is inadequate prep work. If the trim wasn't properly cleaned, sanded, or primed, especially if it had old oil-based paint, the new paint just won't adhere well. Think of it like trying to stick tape to a dusty surface – it just won't hold! Another issue can be skipping the right primer, particularly on challenging surfaces or when making a significant color change. Also, not allowing enough drying time between coats can cause problems, leading to a weak film that's prone to chipping. If your trim has intricate details or heavy wear, these areas are even more susceptible to peeling if not treated right. Sometimes, it's about the paint itself – using a low-quality product or one not suited for trim can be a factor. If you've been battling peeling trim, it might be time to bring in someone who deals with these challenges regularly. HH Remodeling LLC has seen it all and can help get your trim looking sharp and staying that way. We're here to make sure your paint job lasts.",
